00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:41.588
- Wizards of the Coast is here.

00:02:41.588 --> 00:02:44.507
- These are like the engineers
of our childhood imagination.

00:02:44.507 --> 00:02:46.866
- They inspired a whole generation,

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:49.501
a whole genre of gaming.

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:51.130
- We play Magic eight hours a day

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.532
and we still want to go to work everyday.

00:02:53.532 --> 00:02:54.690
- I am super excited
- Yes?

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.010
- to teach Buzzfeed
people how to play Magic.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.475
- Magic is a game of threats and answers.

00:03:00.475 --> 00:03:02.572
You're gonna play creatures
to threaten your opponent.

00:03:02.572 --> 00:03:04.798
Your opponent is gonna defend themselves.

00:03:04.798 --> 00:03:09.224
This will continue until one
of you emerges victorious.

00:03:09.224 --> 00:03:10.727
- Oh (bleep).

00:03:10.727 --> 00:03:13.864
I think I'm officially a Magic convert.

00:03:13.864 --> 00:03:16.158
- The person helping us, Melissa.

00:03:16.158 --> 00:03:18.525
After a while, she was
giving us less instructions

00:03:18.525 --> 00:03:20.829
'cause we were able to actually go

00:03:20.829 --> 00:03:22.024
with the flow of the game.

00:03:22.024 --> 00:03:23.141
- Everything I taught them, they were like

00:03:23.141 --> 00:03:24.186
"Oh my god, I get it.

00:03:24.186 --> 00:03:25.726
"Oh my god, it hit me.

00:03:25.726 --> 00:03:26.995
"I understand."

00:03:26.995 --> 00:03:29.250
- One hit, she decides to take the hit

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.825
instead of this card dying.

00:03:30.825 --> 00:03:32.891
- The strategy behind
it really was up to you

00:03:32.891 --> 00:03:35.344
